/target
/.codesage/
*.db
.plan/
/notes/
/.claude/
/.claude-cycles/

# Benchmark artifacts. Tracked content under bench/ is infrastructure only
# (runner script, extractor, cleanup). Results, corpora, history, and
# scorecards stay local so private-repo names and case IDs never reach a
# commit by accident.
#
# bench/public-corpus-results/ is the deliberate exception and is TRACKED. It
# holds results over published third-party corpora only, where the repo names
# are already public and no query text or case IDs are stored. It is a separate
# directory rather than a filename pattern under bench/history/ because a
# pattern like `semble-*.json` would also match a private run someone named
# `semble-private-client.json`; a directory makes the contract checkable.
/bench/results-*
/bench/corpora/
/bench/history/
/bench/private/
/bench/*.scorecard.md
/bench/analyze-*.py

# Secrets and credentials. Never track these. The pre-commit leak check
# enforces the same policy with filename + content regex; this list is
# the front door so `git add -A` can't sweep them in.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.template
!.env.sample
.secret
.secrets
.secrets/
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
id_dsa*
id_ecdsa*
id_ed25519*
credentials.json
service-account*.json
__pycache__/
